    "rich_text_Ex4H9z": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_F3D6f7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Multi-media water softeners and filtration systems generally use layers of sand, gravel, and media for water treatment. These systems can require plumbing modifications, backwashing, regular servicing, media replacement, and additional installation space.</p><p>Scale-O Salt-Free Water Softener provides a cleaner and more convenient hard water solution without the hassle of heavy maintenance or water wastage. Its food-grade media technology is designed for simple overhead tank installation with long-lasting performance.</p><h4>Why Scale-O Salt Free Water Softener is Better</h4><ul><li>No backwashing or water wastage unlike multi-media water softeners</li><li>No salt refilling required unlike salt-based water softeners</li><li>No electricity consumption unlike electro-magnetic systems</li><li>No media replacement or recurring maintenance costs</li><li>No plumbing modifications or pipe cutting required</li><li>No bulky external setup taking extra installation space</li><li>No technician or manpower dependency for installation</li><li>DIY installation within minutes inside overhead tanks</li><li>Zero maintenance operation compared to traditional systems</li><li>No regeneration cycles or water loss</li><li>Lower initial investment compared to many traditional water softeners</li><li>Zero operating cost with no salt, power, or servicing expenses</li><li>No valves, motors, or electrical parts that can fail over time</li><li>Compact overhead tank design suitable for Indian homes</li><li>Better long-term savings compared to high-maintenance water softeners</li></ul><h3>5 Year Cost Comparison</h3><h4>Hidden Costs of Traditional Hard Water Softeners</h4><p>Most homeowners only compare the initial price of a water softener system. However, long-term ownership costs can become very expensive. </p><h5>Estimated 5-Year Ownership Comparison (need to add costing and compare other water softeners) </h5>"
          }
        }
      },
